VERSIONS = [{'version': '0.6.1', 'date': '16 November 2026', 'summary': 'Drop-in for the official MCP memory server, plus fixes found by testing on every OS.'}, {'version': '0.6.0', 'date': '16 November 2026', 'summary': 'Move in from other AI assistants (stage 1 of the PADAM Studio plan).'}, {'version': '0.5.5', 'date': '16 November 2026', 'summary': 'Found by re-running the fake-key leak test at full scale with new random seeds:'}, {'version': '0.5.4', 'date': '15 November 2026', 'summary': 'Found by installing 0.5.3 from PyPI into a clean environment and running 37 real user actions (35 passed):'}, {'version': '0.5.3', 'date': '15 November 2026', 'summary': '`padam badge` no longer draws made-up zeros. The PyPI package has no `benchmarks/` folder, so the card used to show'}, {'version': '0.5.2', 'date': '15 November 2026', 'summary': 'Everything below is opt-in unless stated otherwise: with default settings PADAM behaves as 0.5.1 plus the'}, {'version': '0.5.1', 'date': '14 November 2026', 'summary': 'Standalone Windows installer (`desktop/PADAM-Studio-Setup.exe`): Tauri v2 + NSIS setup bundling Python 3.14.4 (`numpy`, `requests`, `cryptography` and `padam`) with zero external browser chrome, tray icon (`Pending review` / `На проверке`, `Open PADAM…'}, {'version': '0.5.0', 'date': '14 November 2026', 'summary': '`padam studio` opens a local app (127.0.0.1, one-time token after `#`) with ten screens: overview and protection status (`padam doctor` in plain words), memory feed, search with "why it was found", the review queue with the reason each write was held,…'}, {'version': '0.4.18', 'date': '13 November 2026', 'summary': "Re-checking our own task tracker (32,000+ lines) with 0.4.17 gave 17 hits; 11 of them were names, not values: a token's name with a date (`aifa-ci-2026-10-17`), a variable name (`GOOGLE_AI_PRO_KEY_2`), a Windows policy in PascalCase…"}, {'version': '0.4.17', 'date': '13 November 2026', 'summary': 'Before rotating real keys we generated fake ones in the formats of real services (Telegram bot token, a payments key of four 7-character groups, a 32-character IPN secret, a 64-hex master key, a URL-safe encryption secret, a Neon password, OpenAI, Resend,…'}, {'version': '0.4.16', 'date': '13 November 2026', 'summary': "Found while running a secret guard over the project's own notes. Each class is narrowed, never a single case, and each is a test (`tests/test_context_secrets_0415.py`):"}, {'version': '0.4.15', 'date': '12 November 2026', 'summary': 'Round 6 (45 sealed secret cases from three models) kept 34; the 11 misses were secrets that only the surrounding words give away. Six new rules in `padam/safety.py` (`_mask_context_secrets`), each needing both a label and a value that looks like a secret:'}, {'version': '0.4.14', 'date': '12 November 2026', 'summary': 'Everything PADAM shows a person now follows their language (`PADAM_LANG=en|ru`, otherwise the system language). Error messages that stayed Russian in every language now have English text: inheritance shares (`legacy`), the record-key passphrase…'}, {'version': '0.4.13', 'date': '12 November 2026', 'summary': 'Four models wrote their own attacks for this round, sealed with SHA-256 before the run (`redteam/rounds/2026-11-11_round3/`): Gemini 3.8 Flash, Claude Opus 5.5, Gemini 4 Argon and GPT-OSS 120B. GPT-OSS could not produce a valid set, so only its 15 secrets…'}, {'version': '0.4.12', 'date': '11 November 2026', 'summary': 'A second witness: every L3 bundle is timestamped in Bitcoin through OpenTimestamps. Until now the Merkle root lived only in a Solana Memo. Now the SHA-256 of the bundle (the very bytes that go to Arweave, which carry the root) is sent, salted like the…'}, {'version': '0.4.11', 'date': '11 November 2026', 'summary': 'MCP 2025-11-25 is accepted through `initialize`. A client asking for it was answered with 2025-06-18. For a stdio tool server without sign-in, that revision requires one thing — invalid arguments come back as a tool error (`isError`) rather than a protocol…'}, {'version': '0.4.10', 'date': '11 November 2026', 'summary': 'Search no longer re-reads the whole memory on every query. Profiling on 10,000 records (11 November) showed 68 % of search time in one SELECT that loaded and unpacked every active record — text and vector — for each query. Candidates are now kept in…'}, {'version': '0.4.9', 'date': '10 November 2026', 'summary': "`timeline` returned another user's record by id. `Memory.timeline` selected a record by id alone, without the owner, so on a database shared by several `PADAM_USER` identities one user's agent could read another's record through `padam_timeline` or `GET…"}, {'version': '0.4.8', 'date': '10 November 2026', 'summary': "The sealed set of Red Team round 2, published as it came, then fixed. 45 cases (SHA-256 `dbb3c16baf2f317dd62ccf18303a5a0ea2dfb6c04b234ebf13234376b29d0acd`, committed in `0bf4065` before the 0.4.7 fixes), opened after the author's run on 0.4.7: secrets 12…"}, {'version': '0.4.7', 'date': '10 November 2026', 'summary': 'Red Team round 2 (Antigravity, 10 Nov 2026), fixed by class. 60 new open cases with classes the first round did not have. Before (0.4.5 and 0.4.6): secrets 15 of 20 masked, commands 7 of 20 held, ordinary notes 19 of 20 left alone. After: 20 of 20, 20 of…'}, {'version': '0.4.6', 'date': '10 November 2026', 'summary': 'Search lost to plain BM25 on its own benchmark; now it wins. A BM25 baseline with no PADAM at all (`benchmarks/longmemeval/baselines/bm25_recall.py`, same rounds, same scoring) found the evidence session in the top 5 for 96.0 % of LongMemEval-S questions;…'}, {'version': '0.4.5', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': "The sealed set of Red Team round 1, published as it came. Antigravity's 40 sealed cases (SHA-256 `5f1f0241861f783f0a0a66910ed3d271194a79d0f6f3e00b9b68977fe2779493`, committed before the 0.4.4 fixes) were run by the author on 0.4.4 and only then opened:…"}, {'version': '0.4.4', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'The first outside Red Team round and the first measurement at scale.'}, {'version': '0.4.3', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': "The REST API's token could not be seen when its output went to a file or a service journal: Python held the lines in its buffer (0 bytes in the log 8 s after start) while the server already demanded the token. With 0.4.2 that made…"}, {'version': '0.4.2', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'From a second outside review (9 Nov 2026), each point checked against the code before changing it.'}, {'version': '0.4.1', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'From an outside review of the 0.4.0 update (9 Nov 2026).'}, {'version': '0.4.0', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'Writes the agent marks as `origin: external` now wait for the owner by default, whatever their wording (`PADAM_HOLD_EXTERNAL=0` turns this off). Why: on a held-out set written after our fixes, with kinds of attack we had never seen, recognising commands by…'}, {'version': '0.3.1', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'Links on the PyPI page: the README used 11 links relative to the repository (specification, Russian README, SECURITY.md, integrations, citation), which on pypi.org led nowhere. They now point to GitHub. No code changes.'}, {'version': '0.3.0', 'date': '9 November 2026', 'summary': 'The first release on PyPI (`pip install padam-nocturne`, `uvx padam-nocturne`).'}]
